Here is a complete, ready-to-run desktop application in Python called BubbleDirStat (a bubble-based alternative to WinDirStat).
Because this is for your business subject, I designed it with a modern dark-mode dashboard UI and made sure it uses 100% built-in Python libraries (tkinter, os, math, threading). You and your groupmates will not need to install any external packages via pip—it will run immediately on any computer with Python installed.
Key Features Included (Great for Your Presentation!)
Filter Controls: Instantly switch between Both (All), Files Only, or Directories Only using the filter bar at the top—Directly fulfilling your core requirement.
Proportional Bubble Packing: Uses a custom spiral circle-packing algorithm that sizes bubbles based on the file/folder size relative to the current directory and packs the largest items toward the center.
Interactive Drill-Down:
Hover over any bubble to highlight it and inspect its exact size and percentage share.
Single-click a bubble to highlight it in the side-panel ranking table.
