How It Works (Talking Points for Your Business Subject)
If your instructor asks how your app works or how it improves upon existing tools like WinDirStat, here are a few points you can explain:
Visual Ergonomics (Bubbles vs. Treemaps): WinDirStat uses nested rectangles (treemaps) which can become visually cluttered with thousands of tiny rectangles. BubbleDirStat focuses on the current directory level, placing the largest storage hogs dead-center and spiraling smaller items outward so users immediately spot what is eating up their disk space.
Targeted Filtering (Both / Files / Directories): Traditional disk analyzers mix files and folders together. Your app lets users isolate only files or only subdirectories with a single click, recalculating relative percentages on the fly.
